b</label><p> higher ratings indicate more costs;</p></fn><fn id="tfn20-ijerph-06-00361"><label>c</label><p> Scored on 3-point scales, higher ratings indicate that barriers are less of a problem;</p></fn><fn id="tfn21-ijerph-06-00361"><label>d</label><p> Scored on 4-point scales, higher ratings indicate less effectiveness and less activity respectively;</p></fn><fn id="tfn22-ijerph-06-00361"><label>e</label><p> Scored on 5-point scales, higher ratings indicate more (higher level of) input (e.g. from advice only, to develop, recommend, or approve the partnership&#x02019;s budget, goals, comprehensive plan).</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="t4-ijerph-06-00361" position="float"><label>Table 4.</label><caption><p>Leadership Skills Score by participation costs to benefits ratio.</p></caption><table frame="box" rules="all"><thead><tr><th align="left" rowspan="2" colspan="1">LSC</th><th align="center" colspan="5" rowspan="1">Comparison of difficulties with benefits of being a CP member</th></tr><tr><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Many more difficulties than benefits</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">A few more difficulties than benefits</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">About the same amount of difficulties and benefits</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">A few more benefits than difficulties</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Many more benefits than difficulties</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Low to Moderate</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">37.4</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">18.3</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">22.9</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">14.5</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">6.9</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">High</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">20.7</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">19.2</td><td align="center" rowspan="1